rince of Wales by the British.", "extract_html": "<p>The <b>Royal Palace Park</b>, also known as <b>Wales Park</b>, <b>Wace Park</b> or <b>Rajawasala Park</b>, is a small park on top a small hill in the heart of the city of Kandy, that overlooks the Kandy Lake and most of the city. Established by King Sri Vikrama Rajasinha of Sri Lanka it was renamed as Wales Park in honor of the Prince of Wales by the British.</p>"}